OL,3,ANorth Korea publishes photos of Kim
OL,4,AJong Un - why do rumours of his death
OL,5,Akeep coming back?
OL,6,
OL,7,FKim Jong Un has appeared in North
OL,8,FKorean state media looking remarkably
OL,9,Fhealthy for a man rumoured to have died
OL,10,Ffrom a brain haemorrhage.
OL,12,FPhotographs published by state
OL,13,Fnewspaper Rodong Sinmun show the
OL,14,F42-year-old dictator touring what the
OL,15,Fpaper said was a clothing and footwear
OL,16,Fexhibition with his daughter.
OL,18,FThe images emerged hours after a
OL,19,FChinese dissident who lives in the US
OL,20,Fclaimed, without evidence, that Kim had
OL,21,Fbeen taken to a hospital in Beijing in
OL,22,Fa coma and had died.
OL,23,APub: 20-OctQpppppppppppppppppppppG10/40
